+# Protocol v2 adapter handoff (2026-10-29)
+
+Native collaboration message relay returned `Native hook relay unavailable`; this file records the coordinated API so transport owners can integrate against actual sources.
+
+```java
+FrameWriter sessionWriter = new FrameWriter(socket.getOutputStream(), () -> closeExactRawSocket(socket), 10000);
+FrameReader reader = sessionWriter.handshake(socket.getInputStream());
+// handshake sends v2 Hello, waits under its own absolute deadline, binds both fresh challenge nonces.
+listener.onConnected();
+listener.onPacket(new Packet.Hello(Codec.PROTO_VERSION)); // consumed Hello, notify dispatcher after reset
+// Only now start keepalive and normal read loop. No extra Hello write.
+```
+
+Alternative low-level APIs: writer.getEpoch(); new FrameReader(input,writer.getEpoch()); writer.write(Hello(v2)); reader.readNext() must be Hello; writer.bindPeerEpoch(reader.getPeerEpoch()). Low-level handshake needs its own independent raw-close deadline. The one-arg FrameReader is deliberately unbound and rejects connection frames. Header is31 bytes: magic/version/type/length/senderEpoch64/seq64/recipientEpoch64. Initial Hello has seq0,recipient0; all later frames echo peer's fresh challenge and strictly increment sequence. A whole recorded session cannot replay on a fresh reader's different local challenge. This framing is not authentication; secure bonded peer-bound transport remains required.
+
+Packet.Progress adds11th `fixAgeMs` argument; old overloads default Integer.MAX_VALUE (unknown/stale); FRESH_FIX_MAX_AGE_MS=10000. Distances/ETA are signed-positive32-bit up to2,147,483,647, with -1 unknown only for progress metric fields. TurnBundle cumulative distance never negative. STRAIGHT/ROUNDABOUT kinds added; exit details travel in localized instructionText. Compressed image256KiB cap, payload320KiB, text1024 UTF-8 bytes strict; reject v1/partial/trailing/malformed payload. Wake config0 normalizes15sec, max60sec.
+
+No device or phone Gradle task run by protocol owner. Root wrapper invoked only outer protocol:test/glass-app:assembleDebug. Tests/run results will be appended before final handoff.
+
+## Observed protocol verification
+
+`../scripts/build-glass.sh` completed successfully (outer modules only) after these repairs:53 discovered,52 passed,1 opt-in emulator case skipped; zero failures/errors. Production FrameReader tests cover mandatory Hello, fresh local challenge, recorded whole-session rejection after reconnect, wrong epochs/reordered/duplicate sequences, exact truncation boundaries and chunked input. Production FrameWriter tests use a deliberately blocked OutputStream whose raw-close callback releases a successful late write: deadline still fails, exact callback once, future writes rejected. Silent handshake expires independently. Keepalive ping sender is separately latched: watchdog still fires. TCP loopback test performs real symmetric challenge handshake and sends100 packets. No radio/API19 optical or installed phone proof.
+
+Main wrapper assembled the Glass debug APK concurrently against sibling changes; final artifact hashes/review belong to root integration and should be regenerated after all owners settle. No phone Gradle was invoked.
+
+Final observed run also covers queue residence added by actual FrameWriter, slow-frame transfer age added by actual FrameReader, loopback-only TCP rejection, and rapid stop/restart generation ownership. All53 cases settled with52 PASS/1 SKIP/0 failures. `git diff --check -- protocol` passed. Protocol owner is finished; no active command processes remain.
